  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 154 PM CDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nUnsettled weather will continue on Monday lasting through at least \nthe middle of next week as a series of disturbances pivot across the \nregion. While the severe risk remains uncertain beyond Sunday \nnight/Monday morning, some stronger to briefly severe storms will be \nentirely possible into next week with thunderstorms mainly confined \nto the late afternoon and early evening hours, weakening overnight \nas more stable air moves into the area after sunset. Will continue \nto monitor the severe potential heading into the beginning of next \nweek and through the end of the week. \n\nDue to continued rain chances, cloudy conditions, and increased cold \nair advection into the region, temperatures will remain below normal \nin the mid 60s to low 70s through Thursday (normal in the low 80s). \nHowever, overnight lows will remain near or slightly above normals \n(upper 40s) as clouds and rain after dark will actually result in \nreduced diurnal cooling at night and keep the region slightly \nwarmer. Expect lows to only drop into the upper 40s to mid 50s \nMonday night through Thursday night.",
